 "notes": [
  "globins4.sto: four globins, from the structural alignment of Bashford and colleagues that the User's Guide cites; globins4.hmm was built from it.",
  "fn3.sto, fn3.hmm, Pkinase.sto, Pkinase.hmm: Pfam seed alignments and profiles. The release has older profiles than its alignments: fn3.hmm is PF00041.13, fn3.sto PF00041.20; Pkinase.hmm is PF00069.17, Pkinase.sto PF00069.24 (their #=GF/ACC lines).",
  "MADE1.sto, MADE1.hmm: Dfam DF0000629.2, the human MADE1 transposable element.",
  "globins45.fa: 45 globins; HBB_HUMAN: human beta-haemoglobin (FASTA); 7LESS_DROME: the UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot text record of the Drosophila Sevenless receptor (P13368, entry version 172), which HMMER reads as it is; dna_target.fa: 330 kb of human chromosome 1 (the release does not say which part), with copies of MADE1."
 ],
